---
import QualityLayout from "../../../layouts/QualityLayout.astro";
import { auditEvidence } from "../../../data/quality-2026";
import { deriveMonthly } from "../../../../scripts/quality-case-study-lib.mjs";
const monthly=deriveMonthly(auditEvidence.caseStudy);
const maxMerges=Math.max(...monthly.map(r=>r.nonDependencyMergedPullRequestIds.length),1);
const maxCases=Math.max(...monthly.map(r=>Math.max(r.reportedReleasedIds.length,r.correctedFirstPublishedIds.length)),1);
---
<QualityLayout title="Maintenance timeline — Counterfact" description="Monthly delivery, reported defects, corrections, and known backlog." canonicalPath="/quality/2026/timeline" active="context">
<article class="appendix-page"><header class="appendix-header quality-reading"><p><a href="/quality/2026">Article</a> / Maintenance timeline</p><h1>Delivery and maintenance over two years</h1><p>The complete monthly series puts delivery, defect reports, and corrections on the same calendar. Separate scales and source-linked records make the counts inspectable.</p></header>
<section class="article-figure quality-figure-wide" aria-labelledby="history-heading">
  <div class="figure-heading"><h2 id="history-heading">Two years of delivery and reported problems</h2><p>September 2024–September 3, 2026. Monthly delivery and known released-defect cases are shown on separate scales. September 2026 contains only three days.</p></div>
  <div class="case-monthly" role="img" aria-label="Monthly non-dependency merges, known released-defect reports, and first corrected releases. Exact values and unresolved records are in the table below.">
    <div class="case-month-heading"><span>Month</span><span>Non-dependency PRs</span><span>Reported / corrected cases</span></div>
    {monthly.map(row=>(<div class:list={["case-month-row",{"adoption-month":row.month==='2026-03'}]}>
      <span>{row.month}{row.partial?'*':''}{row.month==='2026-03'?' †':''}</span>
      <span class="case-track"><span class="case-bar" style={`width:${row.nonDependencyMergedPullRequestIds.length/maxMerges*100}%`}></span><b>{row.nonDependencyMergedPullRequestIds.length}</b></span>
      <span class="case-pair"><span class="case-track"><span class="case-bar reported" style={`width:${row.reportedReleasedIds.length/maxCases*100}%`}></span><b>{row.reportedReleasedIds.length}</b></span><span class="case-track"><span class="case-bar corrected" style={`width:${row.correctedFirstPublishedIds.length/maxCases*100}%`}></span><b>{row.correctedFirstPublishedIds.length}</b></span></span>
    </div>))}
  </div>
  <p class="figure-note">† Adoption occurred March 10 at 16:38:20 UTC; the March bar spans both workflows. Pre/post summaries use that exact instant. Teal marks reports; amber marks first corrected publications. These are known, deduplicated cases with supported released status. Unknown release status and unresolved candidates are excluded from those bars and remain visible below. Two direct-mainline candidates have no established discovery instant and cannot be assigned to a month; they remain unresolved in the ledger.</p>
  <details><summary>Exact monthly values, discovery channels, and known backlog</summary><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Monthly observations">
  <table class="research-table"><thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>PRs</th><th>Releases</th><th>External discovery</th><th>Internal human</th><th>Automated / agent</th><th>Unknown discovery</th><th>Corrected</th><th>Known backlog at start</th><th>Pre-release findings</th><th>Unknown release status</th><th>Unresolved candidates</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  {monthly.map(r=><tr><th scope="row">{r.month}{r.partial?' (partial)':''}</th><td>{r.nonDependencyMergedPullRequestIds.length}</td><td>{r.publishedReleaseIds.length}</td><td>{r.reportedReleasedByChannel['external-human']}</td><td>{r.reportedReleasedByChannel['internal-human']}</td><td>{r.reportedReleasedByChannel['automated-agent']}</td><td>{r.reportedReleasedByChannel.unknown}</td><td>{r.correctedFirstPublishedIds.length}</td><td>{r.carryInKnownBacklogIds.length}</td><td>{r.reportedPreReleaseIds.length}</td><td>{r.reportedUnknownReleaseIds.length}</td><td>{r.unresolvedRecordIds.length}</td></tr>)}
  </tbody></table></div></details>
  <p class="figure-note">“Known backlog” means identified public reports awaiting a corrected public release, with supported released status. It excludes unknown and undisclosed defects. A zero in a discovery-channel column is not evidence that no one in that channel found defects: discovery attribution is often unknown. <a href="/quality/2026/candidates#census">Inspect the public-record census.</a></p>
</section><p class="quality-reading"><a href="/quality/2026/candidates">Inspect the case records</a> · <a href="/quality/2026/data.json">Download data</a> · <a href="/quality/2026/methodology">Methods</a></p></article></QualityLayout>
